# Beats script: roast chicken (DLG-1, docs/plans/dialogue-stage.md section 8; the ask is films.json "chicken"). Seconds: chicken.json.
# Read it top to bottom as the conversation. "# you" lines are the person; every other line is what the agent sends.
# A reply is one flow (meta.flow, one row per beat). A beat opens with its spoken line (say) and holds what that line
# changes on screen. The waypoint here is a real wait: the oven takes its time, and the flow holds until it is hot.

# you: Roast a lemon-garlic chicken: the steps and the timing.

# reply 1, flow c1
# beat 1
say "Lemon garlic chicken takes about ninety minutes, and most of it is waiting."
anchor "About 90 minutes, mostly waiting"
shapes w=10 h=4 "Roast chicken" caption="Heat, prep, roast, rest."
shape@oven circle "Oven 220°C" tone=mute
shape arrow
shape@prep box "Prep 15 min" tone=mute
shape arrow
shape@roast pill "Roast 60 min" tone=mute
shape arrow
shape@rest circle "Rest 15 min" tone=mute
# beat 2
say "First, heat the oven to 220 degrees, so it is hot when the bird goes in."
anchor "Oven first: 220°C"
~oven tone=accent +pulse
# beat 3
say "While it heats, rub the bird with butter, garlic and lemon zest, then put the lemon inside."
anchor "Butter, garlic, lemon"
~prep tone=accent
# you cut in during beat 3: wait, I have no lemons. Can I use lime?

# reply 2, flow c2
# beat 4
say "Lime works. Use one lime, not two, because it is sharper."
anchor "Lime works: use one"
~shapes caption="Lime instead of lemon: one is enough."
# beat 5
say "Tell me when the oven is hot, and I will start the roast timer."
wait@hot "Is the oven hot?" "It's hot"|"Not yet"
# you, fifteen minutes later when the oven is hot, tap: It's hot

# reply 3, flow c3
# beat 6
say "In it goes. Sixty minutes, then check that the thigh reads 75 degrees."
anchor "Roast 60 min, thigh 75°C"
~roast tone=accent +pulse
timer@clock 60m "Roast" +inline +auto
# beat 7
say "Then let it rest fifteen minutes before you carve."
anchor "Rest 15 min, then carve"
~rest tone=accent
